Stack is simply a data structure which works on the principle of LIFO(Last in First out) or First in Last out(FILO).It only has one end from where both insertion and deletion takes place.
Stack has some basic functions like
->peek
->top
->isEmpty
->isFull
->push
->pop

Java has inbuilt stack but for better understanding we make custom stack
Code for custom stack->

class Stack{
  int[] data;
  public static final int DEFAULT_SIZE = 10;
  int top = -1;

  public Stack(){
    this(DEFAULT_SIZE);
  }
  public Stack(int size){
    this.data = new int[size];
  }

  public boolean isEmpty(){
    if(top == -1){
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
  public boolean isFull(){
    return top == data.length-1;
  }
  public void push(int item){
    if(isFull()){
      System.out.println("Stack Overflow");
      return;
    }
    top++;
    data[top] = item;
    return;
  }
  public int pop(){
    if(isEmpty()){
      System.out.println("Stack UnderFLow");
      return -1;
    }
    int removed = data[top];
    top--;
    return removed;
  }
  public int peek(){
    if(isEmpty()){
      System.out.println("Stack UnderFLow");
      return -1;
    }
    return data[top];
  }
}















